# ARCHITECTURAL RULES & CODE CONVENTIONS

## 1. Syntax & Formatting Constraints
- ALWAYS use 2-space indentation. NEVER use tabs.
- ALWAYS use single quotes (`'`) for string literals and JSX props.
- Convert double quotes in motion props automatically: `type='spring'`.
- Format spring transition objects explicitly: `transition={{ type: 'spring', damping: 28, stiffness: 350 }}`.

## 2. TypeScript & Type Safety
- Enforce strict typing. NEVER use `any`.
- Use Discriminated Unions for all domain errors:
  `export type AppError = { category: 'MISSING_FIELD'; key: string } | { category: 'QUOTA_EXHAUSTED'; retryMs: number };`
- Explicitly type React component props with named interfaces.

## 3. Performance & Memory Management
- Offload expensive telemetry/math calculations (FPS variance, array sorting) to Web Workers.
- NEVER run array processing loops over 100+ items directly on the main React thread.
- Isolate re-renders by wrapping heavy row components in `React.memo` with custom `propsAreEqual` comparators.

## 4. API & Error Handling
- Wrap external API calls (e.g. Gemini / backend endpoints) in circuit breakers to handle HTTP 429 quota exhaustion gracefully.
- Return fallback payloads when rate limits engage instead of throwing uncaught rejections.
